Remove the top-level VERSION file.

Windows file systems are case-insensitive and MSVC has no separate quote
include path, so Bazel's `-iquote external/usearch+` becomes `/I`, and every
`#include <version>` in a dependent target (e.g. via <assert.h> in the UCRT)
resolves to this file instead of the C++ standard header. Nothing in the
Bazel build reads it.

diff --git a/VERSION b/VERSION
deleted file mode 100644
--- a/VERSION
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1 +0,0 @@
-2.26.4
